    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="61ea9ea5-e096-5c53-9f2a-a2dbf92fd959" activityNameId="7ce7c394-7d02-55af-a7d1-d13538beaae2" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Plasticiser, for concrete, based on sulfonated melamine formaldehyde</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Plasticiser, for concrete, based on sulfonated melamine formaldehyde
This dataset contains the production of a plasticiser for concrete based on sulfonated melamine formaldehyde. The activity starts with the ingredients for the plasticiser at the factory gate. The values on energy consumption are generic data (see respective comments fields".\nTechnology: Literature data\nTime period: Time of publications.\nVersion: 1\nEnergy values: Undefined\nLocal category: Mineralische Baustoffe\nLocal subcategory: Zuschlags- Füllstoffe\nUVEK 2022 source file:551-Zement-Klinker_v0.9._Fliessmittel.xml\n\n
UUID: 254f47f0-4721-37e2-bf58-dfeab05fdc27
Plasticisers or water reducers, and superplasticiser or high range water reducers, are chemical admixtures that can be added to concrete mixtures to improve workability. Plasticisers are commonly manufactured from lignosulfonates, a by-product from the paper industry. Superplasticisers have generally been manufactured from sulfonated naphthalene condensate or sulfonated melamine formaldehyde, although newer products based on polycarboxylic ethers are now available.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Literature data
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: &lt;null&gt;
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_254f47f0-4721-37e2-bf58-dfeab05fdc27.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
